  "intentional_differences": [
    "Non-secret keys in C:\\HC\\config now match the live NSSM environment, including GLENN_UPLOADER_INGEST_ENABLED (TKP, TCP, and AGM true; YQ false), TCP PYTHONPATH=C:\\HC\\apps\\shared;C:\\HC\\apps\\tcp, and no TCP_V2_SKIP_BENCHMARK_FETCH on the service or in tcp.env.",
    "The config files omit secret variable names. Live NSSM still loads DOWNSTREAM_INGEST_TOKEN, GLENN_UPLOADER_INGEST_TOKEN, TCP_V2_ADMIN_TOKEN, and TCP_V2_SESSION_SECRET. Importing a config file alone would drop those secrets.",
    "C:\\HC\\config\\uploader\\uploader.env matches the live non-secret uploader variables and omits DOWNSTREAM_INGEST_TOKEN. The running service has that variable. No C:\\HC\\secrets env file defines it. C:\\HC\\secrets\\uploader\\README.txt says it was not copied. Automatic backups do not include secret values.",
    "HC-YQ-Public has one empty NSSM AppEnvironmentExtra entry. The catalog ignores it and a future recreate will not add it.",
    "Cloudflared is a native Windows service. Its ImagePath is cloudflared.exe, not nssm.exe, and it has no NSSM Application parameter. A future recreate on a new host uses sc.exe. This catalog does not change Cloudflare DNS.",
    "Display names remain the live strings, including 'HC Uploader Public (private, writes disabled)' and 'HC TCP Public (private pilot)'. Writer authority is the environment: TKP, TCP, and AGM ingest enabled; YQ ingest disabled; uploader EXPORT_INCLUDE_YQ=false.",
    "HC-TCP-Public runs as .\\svc_hc_tearsheets. The account password is not stored here. -Apply on a new host requires HC_SVC_HC_TEARSHEETS_PASSWORD and must not print it. -DryRun does not need it.",
    "TKP, TCP, YQ, and AGM use C:\\HC\\apps\\shared\\.venv310\\Scripts\\python.exe as the NSSM application and the script path as AppParameters. Uploader uses C:\\HC\\apps\\uploader\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. That is the live split.",
    "The on-disk AGM launcher is an absolute-path runpy script. Git commit 5ca9a7c6419559ae1375d8b4adb5533bc0ba16c5 is the repo-relative launcher. Service parity is the live command line.",
    "Deployed yq_ts.py is not a byte-for-byte copy of git 7a935e4e66bcd0983b4ccc7cb962eafeb6db59c0 (UTF-8 BOM, trailing newline, CP437 mojibake). Recovery uses the git file. tearsheet_paths.py comes from 0a157c49d769202c1c92590d6acc31ca512588fc.",
    "HC-TCP-Public was re-read from Win32_Service and Parameters after the 2026-10-10 recycle. Application remains C:\\HC\\apps\\shared\\.venv310\\Scripts\\python.exe, AppParameters remains C:\\HC\\apps\\tcp\\tcp_ts_v2.py, and AppDirectory remains C:\\HC\\apps\\tcp. The NSSM python child uses that command line and re-execs C:\\Python310\\python.exe with the same script; the re-exec listens on 127.0.0.1:8302. Uploader, TKP, YQ, and AGM use the same venv re-exec pattern. Process ids are not catalog fields. Do not restart a service to chase them."
  ],
